   * To rotate, put the new password first and the old one after it: sessions
   * sealed with the old one keep working and are resealed with the new one as
   * users browse. The old password has no expiry, so removing it once the window
   * closes is an operational decision, not something the code does. Each entry
   * adds up to two PBKDF2 derivations for every invalid cookie, so keep the list
   * short.
   *
